(How it works:) '
(Win, then block: it tries each legal column for the AI first, then for the opponent. It) '
(plays the first column that wins, or blocks if the opponent could win there. Winning is) '
(checked before blocking, so the AI never blocks when it could simply win.) '
(Safe fallback: it skips any column where the AI's piece would let the opponent win by) '
(stacking on top of it. If every move is unsafe, it plays a legal one anyway rather than) '
(returning nothing. Among the safe moves it prefers the center columns, which are stronger) '
(in Connect Four, and picks randomly among ties.) '
(Full columns: only columns whose top cell is "." are considered, and drop returning None) '
(is treated as "not a win". If the board is full the method returns None, which the game) '
(loop already handles.) '
(No board mutation: each trial runs on copy.deepcopy\(board\), because I don't know whether) '
(your Board has an undo method. If it has a cheap undo or a copy method, swap that in for) '
(speed. With 7 columns the deepcopy cost doesn't matter.) '
